---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Blorg"
	summary="An interactive workspace for exploring computer science classics — powered by Astro, React, and LIPS."
	createTime={new Date('May 30 2026')}
>
	<p>
		<strong>Blorg</strong> is an interactive learning workspace that transforms classic computer science texts
		into living documents. Code blocks become executable cells; the reader edits and runs them in place.
	</p>

	<h2>How it works</h2>

	<p>
		Built on Astro 6 for static content delivery, with React 19 powering the interactive code cells.
		The Scheme/Lisp interpreter runs entirely in the browser via the LIPS library — no server backend needed.
		Content is authored in <strong>Org-mode</strong>, a structured markup format designed for literate programming.
	</p>

	<h2>Key features</h2>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Interactive cells</strong> — every code block is a CodeMirror 6 editor. Press Cmd+Enter to run.</li>
		<li><strong>Global console</strong> — all execution output collects in a Jupyter-style log at the bottom of the screen.</li>
		<li><strong>Glassmorphism UI</strong> — clean, minimal workspace design with no distraction.</li>
		<li><strong>Offline-capable</strong> — code sessions persist to Origin Private File System (OPFS).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Roadmap</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Multi-language support (Python via Pyodide, Haskell, etc.)</li>
		<li>Collaborative annotations</li>
		<li>Session save/restore with workspace history</li>
	</ul>
</Layout>